# Motion

- Durations come from tokens only: `--gx-motion-fast` (120ms), `--gx-motion-base` (200ms),
  `--gx-motion-slow` (360ms). In Tailwind: `duration-(--gx-motion-fast)`. Never `duration-300`.
- Transition or animate only `translate`, `scale`, `rotate`, `transform`, `opacity`. Name the
  property (`transition: translate ...`); never `transition: all` or `transition-all`. Change
  box-shadow, filter and colours instantly instead. `check-css.mjs` enforces this.
- Game feel = stepped timing: `steps(n, end)` for presses, fills and pops; smooth easing only
  where a component is explicitly `-smooth`.
- Reduced motion has two switches and both must work:
  - `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)` zeroes the motion tokens.
  - `data-gx-motion="reduce"` on any ancestor does the same (for an in-app setting).
- Token-timed one-shot animations stop automatically. Infinite animations (sprites, blinking,
  nudging) need an explicit `animation: none` under both switches.
- Motion never carries meaning alone: a blinking critical bar also changes its text label.
- Typewriter text: instant when reduced motion is on; first interact completes the line,
  the next advances.
